 ## Background
-The Vessel Voxelizer is an open-source project hosted on GitHub by faberno [S1, unofficial]. It is implemented using CUDA and Python bindings via `nanobind`. The method is designed for the voxelization of vascular structures, which are typically represented as tree-like graphs of line segments with associated radii. The project includes a demo notebook and a CSV-based input format for vessel data [S1, unofficial].
